  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow faith-intro-eyebrow">An Introduction</p>
      <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">The Second London Baptist Confession, often called the 1689, is the most thorough confession of the Reformed Baptist tradition. Its English drafters worked closely from the Westminster Confession, copying Westminster’s language wherever they agreed and rewriting only on baptism, the church, and civil government. The result is a document that sits inside the Reformed family while staking out a particular polity: believer’s baptism, congregational church order, religious liberty under the civil magistrate.</p>
      <div class="flourish faith-intro-flourish">{{> "flourish-mark"}}</div>
    </div>
  </section>
    
